    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric coating on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2(1)|SiO2(2)|HfO2(3)|SiO2(4)|HfO2(5)|SiO2(6)|HfO2(7)|SiO2(8)|HfO2(9)|SiO2(10)|HfO2(11)|SiO2(12)|HfO2(13)|SiO2(14)|HfO2(15)|SiO2(16)|HfO2(17)|SiO2(18)|HfO2(19)|SiO2(20)|HfO2(21)|SiO2(22)|HfO2(23)|SiO2(24). Initialize thicknesses from baseline values [127.0, 100.0, 121.0, 100.0, 124.0, 178.0, 96.0, 153.0, 116.0, 152.0, 111.0, 101.0, 140.0, 100.0, 116.0, 144.0, 124.0, 100.0, 117.0, 166.0, 104.0, 100.0, 116.0, 108.0] nm. Relax all thickness bounds by ±10% from baseline bounds of 80-400 nm. Apply deterministic coordinate-wise perturbation of ±4.0 nm to worst-performing 25% of candidates each iteration. Use coherent smatrix solver across combined 300-1700 nm wavelength range. Optimize for mean transmittance in 1000-1700 nm band and mean reflectance in 300-450 nm band simultaneously. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: low transmission in 300-450 nm; low reflection in 1000-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count <= 30; materials restricted to HfO2 and SiO2.",
